{"w": 595.3200073242188, "h": 809.0257568359375, "lines": [{"t": "87", "x": 0.9036148555787364, "y": 0.9742087522985531, "w": 0.03012839302489931, "h": 0.017428414981790374, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Initially, this process was invented to keep Australian beer cool even in hot", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.12319506908974809, "w": 0.825924649490251, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "weather. But Australian cattlemen were quick to realize that, if they could put this", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.15152541916388573, "w": 0.8261206772019258, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "new invention on a ship, they could export meat across the oceans. In 1880, a", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.17970752416545568, "w": 0.8261885487213446, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "shipment of Australian beef and mutton was sent, frozen, to England. While the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2080378742395933, "w": 0.8260987368618117, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "food frozen this way was still palatable, there was some deterioration. During the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.23636822431373095, "w": 0.8262728242333722, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "freezing process, crystals formed within the cells of the food, and when the ice", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.26469857438786853, "w": 0.8264092849468865, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "expanded and the cells burst, this spoilt the flavor and texture of the food.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2930660423122369, "w": 0.7597011161789196, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "The modern frozen food industry began with the indigenous Inuit people of", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.33133430071101805, "w": 0.8259682225956181, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Canada. In 1912, a biology student in Massachusetts, USA, named Clarence", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3596646507851557, "w": 0.8267030189395372, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Birdseye, ran out of money and went to Labrador in Canada to trap and trade furs.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.38799500085929334, "w": 0.8262294561779128, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "While he was there, he became fascinated with how the Inuit would quickly freeze", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.41632538865482344, "w": 0.8262949696233941, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "fish in the Arctic air. The fish looked and tasted fresh even months later.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4446557764503536, "w": 0.7345046347943242, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Birdseye returned to the USA in 1917 and began developing mechanical freezers", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.48280040298518045, "w": 0.8261245731501704, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "capable of quick-freezing food. Birdseye methodically kept inventing better", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5111307907807106, "w": 0.8262162304588719, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "freezers and gradually built a business selling frozen fish from Gloucester,", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5394611408548482, "w": 0.8259899578858247, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Massachusetts. In 1929, his business was sold and became General Foods, but he", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5677915286503784, "w": 0.8264450661557643, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "stayed with the company as director of research, and his division continued to", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5961219164459085, "w": 0.8259031192499521, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "innovate.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6244523042414386, "w": 0.09720029469772722, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Birdseye was responsible for several key innovations that made the frozen food", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6627576239083618, "w": 0.8261207797268797, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "industry possible. He developed quick-freezing techniques that reduced the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6909396534671467, "w": 0.8265035053794331, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "damage that crystals caused, as well as the technique of freezing the product in", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7192700035412843, "w": 0.8259029142000445, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.747600429058207, "w": 0.038751049214746, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "package it was to be sold in. He also introduced the use of cellophane, the first", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8241369081343769, "w": 0.8260552662813984, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "transparent material for food packaging, which allowed consumers to see the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8524672582085145, "w": 0.8265285214681615, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "quality of the product. Birdseye products also came in convenient size packages", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8806740330007866, "w": 0.825968325120572, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "that could be prepared with a minimum of effort.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.9090043830749241, "w": 0.49780840095622975, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}], "source": "pdf text layer"}